From 77457e60b746480ef2c1705706aa9a3f5b17ae5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sahan Nissanka <adee.sahan@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 17:00:56 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: simple: awb: Widen the colour gain range to UQ<3, 8>

The software ISP bounds its AWB colour gains with a fixed-point format,
UQ<2, 8>, capping them at 3.996. AwbAlgorithmBase::process() clamps every
computed result to that ceiling, so a sensor that needs more can never be
white balanced and sits permanently short of neutral.

As the comment on the member notes, there is no register format behind
this choice. The software ISP carries the gains as double throughout:
DebayerParams::gains is an RGB<double>, and DebayerCpu builds its lookup
tables in double, clamping only the table index rather than the gain. The
bound is therefore free to be chosen, and 3.996 is too low for real
sensors.

On an OV5675 (Dell Latitude 7320 Detachable, IPU6, software ISP) pointed
at lit white paper, the raw Bayer response with the black level subtracted
is R/G 0.164 and B/G 0.665, so reaching neutral needs a red gain of 6.1.
Against the previous hardcoded 4.0 clamp the red gain pinned at the
ceiling on every frame while blue computed normally at 1.55, leaving a
cyan cast; the 3.996 ceiling has the same effect.

Widen the format to UQ<3, 8>, which raises the ceiling to 7.996 and leaves
headroom for similarly red-weak sensors.

Signed-off-by: Sahan Nissanka <adee.sahan@gmail.com>
---
 src/ipa/simple/algorithms/awb.h | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/awb.h b/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/awb.h
index ff0a7a28..77478e6d 100644
--- a/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/awb.h
+++ b/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/awb.h
@@ -52,11 +52,13 @@ private:
 					 const SwIspStats *stats) const;
 
 	/*
-	 * There actually is no Q register format for SoftISP, but allow the
-	 * colour gains to range in the [0.0f, 3.999f] interval, which seems
-	 * reasonable.
+	 * There actually is no Q register format for SoftISP, so the format
+	 * only serves to bound the gains. UQ<2, 8> caps them at 3.996, which
+	 * is too low: an OV5675 has a red response of 0.164 relative to green
+	 * and needs a red gain of 6.1 to reach neutral. UQ<3, 8> raises the
+	 * ceiling to 7.996 and leaves room for similarly red-weak sensors.
 	 */
-	AwbAlgorithm<UQ<2, 8>> awbAlgo_;
+	AwbAlgorithm<UQ<3, 8>> awbAlgo_;
 };
 
 } /* namespace ipa::soft::algorithms */
